bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27, 0, "Seed JIT: pushing a u64 >= 2^63 into a [u64] array stores it with bit 62 flipped; index stores, literals and [i64] pushes are exact. Broke Argon2id on the JIT once argon2 stopped demoting to the interpreter."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27, P2, open, "Seed JIT [u64].push flips bit 62 for values >= 2^63", doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27.md, 1, doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27.md, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 reproduced on aarch64 DGX with seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b (interpret exact, jit xor=0x4000000000000000). Workaround in src/lib/common/crypto/argon2.spl (pre-sized index-assigned [u64] buffers); RFC 9106 5.3 vector passes on both engines."
